You was running down the night streets as fast as you could, and soon many-storied buildings were changed by small private houses. You found a broken half-ruined shack and decided to wait there for dawn. You rolled yourself up into a ball and fell asleep. The morning chill woke you up at the crack of dawn. You sneaked in the neighboring courtyard and took a shirt and a pair of trousers that dried on the ropes. You quickly dressed up and headed towards the highway. But the most important question was what or who made you turn into a wolf. You was absolutely sure, that no animal bit or even scratch you. You was confused. As ill luck would have it, there were no cars on the road when you badly needed to get home. Moreover, you was hungry again. You saw a bar for truck drivers behind the trees, and decided to go there.